('be67401f-df2e-44c1-ab60-b18ce26551de','13a881b0-3c1c-4f36-8449-76e1f13b9505','7f5a145c-4614-4e8f-b64d-c6265ce44f4a','Working','Working','Working','Working','Working',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-11-05 13:54:13','2026-11-05 13:54:13'),
('d0865dda-512a-4682-89c9-d46803e79bc9','4a14c978-bfd5-11f1-9638-5bc6d2c76fd7','6e11697b-f6d3-4a3f-a4d9-e113b583c5ac','During my internship at Nexus Embedded Systems, a semiconductor and IoT solutions provider, I served as a Firmware Engineering Intern. I worked within the hardware-software integration team, consisting of three hardware design engineers, two embedded systems developers, and a quality assurance lead. Collaborating across teams taught me that computer engineering requires a flawless bridge between physical circuitry and system software. I learned how hardware limitations directly dictate code optimization and how strict safety standards guide hardware deployment.','My schedule was a strict on-site arrangement from Monday to Friday, 8:30 AM to 5:30 PM, completing 40 hours per week due to lab equipment dependencies. My core responsibilities included writing low-level C drivers for microcontroller peripherals, using digital oscilloscopes and logic analyzers to debug hardware signals, and running automated regression testing on system firmware. I also updated internal hardware registers documentation and participated in weekly schematic design reviews.','My most memorable moment occurred when I successfully debugged a persistent timing synchronization flaw between a microprocessor and an external flash memory module. By analyzing SPI bus signals on a logic analyzer, I located a microsecond signal delay mismatch and corrected it in the driver firmware. Watching the bare-metal system boot up cleanly without a single communication error for the first time was incredibly rewarding. This moment cemented my passion for low-level problem solving where software directly manipulates hardware.','The primary challenge I faced was learning to read complex circuit schematics and mapping them accurately to register-level code, which was far more intricate than high-level programming. To resolve this, I spent extra time studying the microcontroller\'s 1,200-page datasheet and cross-referencing PCB layout files using Altium Designer. I also sought guidance from a senior hardware engineer, who taught me how to isolate hardware faults from software bugs. This obstacle sharpened my technical literacy and taught me a structured, logical approach to debugging system-level failures.','This photo shows my engineering workbench inside the hardware testing lab, surrounded by my development boards, a digital oscilloscope, and testing leads. On the monitor is the terminal output displaying a successful build and execution of the microchip driver firmware I rewrote. This image represents the hands-on engineering skills, analytical patience, and technical precision I developed during my hardware-software integration training.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-28 11:51:55','2026-10-28 11:51:55'),
('dded315b-12de-4a26-afcb-37b26cebd49c','2995a6d2-2371-4127-8841-dd2cf87dae27','ad760dbb-12ba-4308-b8f5-29fae4cb01cc','During my internship at Phoenix Petroleum Philippines, I served as a Data Analyst Intern. Throughout this experience, I had the privilege of working closely with a highly collaborative and supportive team of professionals, particularly my supervisor, and my fellow team members. They consistently provided valuable guidance, welcomed my questions, and included me in core departmental meetings. Through this immersive workplace environment, I learned the critical importance of cross-functional communication, adaptability in fast-paced settings, and how corporate strategies translate into daily operational tasks.','My regular work schedule was structured from Monday through Friday, spanning 40 hours per week from 8:00 AM to 5:00 PM. My primary daily responsibilities included managing data entry updates, conducting weekly market research, and assisting the core team with drafting project summaries and client presentations. I was also responsible for attending daily morning stand-up syncs to align on project timelines, manage my task queues efficiently, and ensure all my weekly deliverables were submitted accurately and on time.','The most memorable moment of my practicum occurred when our team successfully launched the mid-quarter marketing campaign. This specific experience stayed with me because it was the first time I saw the direct, tangible impact of my hard work contributing to a major company milestone. Receiving positive, constructive feedback from senior leadership greatly boosted my professional confidence. It made me feel like a truly valued member of the team rather than just an observer, solidifying my passion for pursuing a long-term career in this field.','One of the main challenges I faced during the early weeks of my internship was balancing multiple tight deadlines simultaneously. To handle this difficulty, I took a proactive approach by  implementing strict time-management blocks and using digital planners / scheduling brief troubleshooting syncs with senior peers. This systematic approach allowed me to overcome the learning curve and keep my projects on track. Through this challenge, I learned the immense value of proactive communication, resourcefulness, and effective problem-solving under pressure.','This section features a group photograph taken on my final day with the team at the office. It serves as a meaningful reminder of the welcoming environment, mentorship, and professional relationships that defined my entire internship experience',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-10-14 17:48:39','2026-11-03 23:38:25');
